<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Hafs Umar I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1295">1295</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Abu Hafs Umar ibn Yahya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Hafs Umar I was the Hafsid sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> from 1284 to 1295, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-zakariya-yahya-i">Abu Zakariya Yahya I</a>. He took power after overthrowing the usurper Ibn Abi Umara, but his nephew Abu Zakariya set up a rival Hafsid state at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Béjaïa</a> in 1285 that refused to recognise him. His reign saw the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djerba">Djerba</a> to the Aragonese admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-of-lauria">Roger of Lauria</a>.</p></div>
